.TH TINTFETCH 1 "November 2026" "Tintfetch" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tintfetch \- display system information and colorful distribution artwork
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tintfetch
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Tintfetch is a Go system information utility. The native engine displays
available information and skips unavailable optional probes. External commands
have a bounded execution time. Output redirected to a file is plain text by default.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR --help
Show all registered options. Some options require an upstream engine.
.TP
.BR --version
Print the build version without probing hardware or reading configuration.
.TP
.BR --config " PATH"
Read the selected configuration. Explicit options override configuration values.
.TP
.BR --no-config
Ignore user and system configuration. No configuration is created automatically.
.TP
.BR --print-config
Print the default declarative configuration.
.TP
.BR --shell-config
Execute the explicitly selected configuration with Bash. Use only with trusted
files. This grants the configuration the same access as the invoking user.
.TP
.BR --plain
Disable artwork and ANSI styling.
.TP
.BR --json
Print an object containing version and entries. Each entry has label, module,
and value string fields. Artwork and ANSI styling are excluded.
.TP
.BR --preset " NAME"
Apply native color stripes to ASCII artwork.
.TP
.BR --list-presets
List native color presets.
.TP
.BR --engine " native|neofetch|hyfetch"
Select the built-in engine or an installed upstream program. Upstream arguments
are forwarded verbatim, apart from the engine selector. The neofetch engine
prefers neowofetch when available. Upstream engines use their own configuration
and may execute shell code according to their own rules.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/tintfetch/config.conf
User configuration. When XDG_CONFIG_HOME is unset, the operating system's user
configuration directory is used (normally ~/.config on Linux).
.TP
.I /etc/tintfetch/config.conf
System fallback when the user configuration does not exist.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Any nonempty value disables native ANSI color and artwork.
.TP
.B TERM
The value dumb disables automatic styling.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 for success, 1 for a runtime error, 2 for invalid native arguments or configuration.
External engines preserve positive upstream exit statuses.
.SH NOTES
The native engine does not implement all Neofetch or HyFetch behavior. See the
installed compatibility document for supported options and platform limitations.
.SH AUTHORS
Tintfetch contributors; derived in part from Neofetch and HyFetch.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR neofetch (1),
.BR hyfetch (1)
